            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="SAY01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Jean Baptiste</forename>
                        <surname>Say</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1767-01-05">
                        <placeName>France</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1832-11-15"/>
                    <occupation>economist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Jean Baptiste Say, the French political economist, travelled to England in 1814 to study the economic condition of the UK. The
    first entry, 'Say from Slabrendorf' suggests that Say had a note of introduction from, or came at the request or recommendation of  Count Slabrendorf, a Swedish acquaintance
    of Mary Wollstonecraft mentioned in Chapter 7 of Godwin's <title>Memoirs</title>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">See William Godwin, <title>Memoirs of the Author of a Vindication of the Rights of Woman</title>, ed. by Pamela Clemit and 
  Gina Luria (Peterborough, Ont.: Broadview Literary Texts, 2001).</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
